WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.150
(dramatic music)

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.190
- [Narrator] Located in Yemen is a palace

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.560
that appears to have been carved

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.480
from the rock that it sits on.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.370
However, this man-made wonder

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.640
was once just a simple summer home.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.460
Just 10 miles away from
Yemen's capital city of Sanaʽa

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:25.133
is Dar al-Hajar, otherwise
known as Imam's Rock Palace.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.440
In the early days of Yemen's history,

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.380
the country was led by the Imam,

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.110
the Islamic spiritual leader,

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.840
rather than a king or president.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.400
The Rock Palace was built in the 1930s

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.960
by Imam Yahya as his summer residence.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:43.530
However, it is believed to have been

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.253
built over an older palace.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:50.230
The residence is five stories
high, has several balconies

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.713
and its own water supply from a deep well.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.090
It is seen as an example of
traditional Yemen architecture

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.100
due to the patterned
windows, earth-tone coloring

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.543
and protruding exterior decorations.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.280
While tourism in this region
is limited due to conflict,

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:09.810
this palace is both a sanctuary for locals

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.023
and an example of the
man-made beauty of Yemen.

